; minEngine export whitelist - GENERATED, do not hand-edit one line at a time.
; Source: PE import tables of the engine consumers, not the DLL export table.
; Contract: libminengine - release libminEngine.dll and debug libminEngined.dll are ONE
;   contract - external repos import the release name (BUILD-F03 P7 / Q8).
; Regenerate from the in-repo hosts plus the LIVE external product bins (BUILD-F03 Q8):
;   python scripts/audit_dll_exports.py --emit-whitelist minEngine/cmake/minEngine_exports.def \
;       --consumer-dir "../minCraft*/bin"
; The legacy block at the end of this file is preserved verbatim by that command.
; Consumers:
;   ../minCraft-gameplay/bin/libminCraft.dll     160 names
;   ../minCraft-ui/bin/MaximumEditor.exe         578 names
;   ../minCraft-ui/bin/MinCraft.exe                7 names
;   ../minCraft-ui/bin/MinCraftEditor.exe        578 names
;   ../minCraft-ui/bin/VoxelWorldTests.exe        24 names
;   ../minCraft-ui/bin/libminCraft.dll           144 names
;   ../minCraft/bin/MinCraftEditor.exe           573 names
;   ../minCraft/bin/VoxelWorldTests.exe           24 names
;   ../minCraft/bin/libminCraft.dll              130 names
;   minEngine/bin/MaximumEditor.exe              579 names
;   minEngine/bin/SampleEditor.exe               579 names
;   minEngine/bin/SampleGame.exe                   7 names
;   minEngine/bin/libGameModuleStubd.dll          26 names
;   minEngine/bin/libminCraftd.dll               153 names
;   minEngine/bin/minEngineTests.exe             794 names
; Entries: 654 (knife2 batch1–3; batch3 burned Reflection/StaticClass off .def; 5 legacy remain)
; BUILD-F04 S04: the imgui bucket left this file together with the sources that defined it
; (253 entries: 224 IMGUI_API + 20 IMGUI_IMPL_API + 9 ImGuizmo, GImGui included as DATA).
; imgui is compiled by libMaximumEditord.dll now. This block keeps 993 entries, the legacy
; block keeps 5. The engine src had 0 imgui calls, so no in-repo consumer loses a symbol: an
; editor host rebuilt against this engine links imgui from the editor DLL.
; BUILD-F04 S04 step 2: the glfw bucket (8 entries) left the contract because the engine no
;   longer DEFINES glfw - it imports the prebuilt glfw3.dll (minengine_glfw), the same DLL the
;   editor DLL imports, so the process has exactly one GLFW instance.
; BUILD-F03 C1 target state for glfw is therefore reached early.
; BUILD-F03 knife 1: the glad bucket (5 entries: GLAD_GL_VERSION_4_6 DATA, gladLoadGLLoader,
;   glad_glBindTexture/glad_glGetError/glad_glGetTexImage DATA) left the contract too. The engine
;   still COMPILES glad.c (GLFWWindowSystem.cpp loads GL through it) but no longer EXPORTS it:
;   the only consumer was minEngineTests, which now carries its own glad translation unit, and
;   a second glad copy inside one process is the state glfw knife 1 removed for GLFW.
