; ==== BEGIN LEGACY-EXTERNAL-DEBT - preserved verbatim by --emit-whitelist ====
; API debt, NOT a derived set. These 5 entries exist for exactly one reason: the LIVE external
; product repos (minCraft / minCraft-ui / minCraft-gameplay) import them today, so removing them
; from the contract breaks their next build. They are not a public API promise.
; Removal condition: an external repo consumes the public replacement below and ships a rebuild,
; after which "audit_dll_exports.py --verify-coverage --consumer-dir <live bin>" stays at 0
; missing with the entry deleted.
; Classification source: BUILD-F03 "consumer misuse list"
; (docs/ai/Platform/ProductBuild/BUILD-F03_SYMBOL_CONTRACT_ROLLOUT_DESIGN.md), entries M10,
; the codegen ABI class D and M5. Keep this block ASCII-only: it is linker input.
;
; [M10 family] SubsystemCollectionBase::InitializeDependency(MEClass const*)
;   Reflection/subsystem wiring of the SubsystemCollectionBase derivation face (M10): internal,
;   reached only through generated subsystem code. Imported by all three product modules.
;   Replacement: declare the codegen entry points MINENGINE_API once F03 slice 2 lands, instead
;   of exporting the raw internal method.
; [codegen class D] T::StaticClass() for the UI/asset types the editor module owns
;   Generated reflection codegen symbols never declared as API (F03 codegen symbols:
;   StaticClass()/GetClassName<T>). Consumers should reach the MEClass through GetClass<T>()/
;   reflection registration instead of naming the generated static directly. Imported by
;   minCraft-ui only.
; [M5-type data debt] LogUI - the console singleton
;   Already exported through MINENGINE_API (dllexport), so listing it here changes nothing at
;   link time; it is listed so the contract states the truth instead of relying on the macro.
;   DATA is mandatory: a .def data export without DATA emits a code thunk that collides with the
;   COMDAT copy consumers emit themselves (S01 V4). Imported by minCraft-ui only.
; ==== END LEGACY-EXTERNAL-DEBT ====
